 "title": "Class-level readings of a learned knot memory are monotone; a negation needs a frame",
 "subject": "Whether networks of knots and parity names can negate a stored bit",
 "conclusion": "A reading that depends only on the stored classes, by any network whose other constraints leave the leaves' signs alone, is non-decreasing in every acting bit and cannot tell non-acting classes apart (proved by hand, by a gauge on the leaf's inner points). A negation exists only for one fixed signing per class, a frame learning's path decides (computed).",
